## Contract workflow

1. Change the authoritative contract FIRST: `<FILL ME — evidence: contract/schema files>`.
2. Update client models/serializers in `<FILL ME — evidence: client model files>`.
3. Update server handlers + validators in `<FILL ME — evidence: server handler files>`.
4. Add negative-path tests for malformed payloads and expired tokens (list concrete cases: <FILL ME — evidence: existing test files>).

## Error mapping

- Client errors are thrown as `<FILL ME — evidence: service error classes>` from `<FILL ME — evidence: service layer files>`.
- The BFF maps provider errors to `<FILL ME — evidence: error-map file>` in `<FILL ME — evidence: the relevant source file>`.
- NEVER log: `<FILL ME — evidence: logging configuration>`.

## Auth boundaries

- Client holds the refresh/access token in `<FILL ME — evidence: client storage/service config>`; never in logs or caches.
- Server validates `<FILL ME — evidence: middleware configuration>` in `<FILL ME — evidence: the relevant source file>`; authorization rules live in `<FILL ME — evidence: the relevant source file>`.
- Cross-service calls use <FILL ME — evidence: service authentication configuration> — see `<FILL ME — evidence: docs/README or API reference>`.

